atlas institutional
# Honest architectural stubs: named, lineage-tracked, but not yet built. The
# atlas surfaces them via `loss` as no_interaction_contract / unwitnessed rather
# than pretending they exist. They are the next mining targets, not claims.

architecture authority-graph
  canonical_name AuthorityGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Authority
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Who may do what, to what, for what purpose, under what evidence, until when?
  purpose Typed authority edges (observe/reference/bind/activate/act/review/approve/commit/delegate/revoke/publish/spend/share/disclose) with scope, expiry, delegation, revocation, evidence.
  maturity implemented
  node_types AuthorityEdge
  node_types Permission
  edge_types delegates
  edge_types revokes
  state_types granted
  state_types expired
  state_types revoked
  internal_calculus in-window non-revoked edge lookup
  internal_calculus scope-constrained delegation
  invariant delegation may compose only under constrained scope
  invariant an edge outside its window or revoked grants nothing
  forbidden_inference affiliation -> authority
  forbidden_inference available -> authorized
  forbidden_inference presence -> authority
  native_format graf
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/authority.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_authority.py
  source_lineage SEED-A recursive organ document

architecture relationship-graph
  canonical_name RelationshipGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Relationship
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Where along the discovery-to-adoption trajectory is this real relationship?
  purpose Not a CRM pipeline: discovered -> observed -> contacted -> replied -> engaged -> assigned -> reviewed -> corrected -> collaborated -> committed -> adopted -> converted. Bernstein/AgentGuard/DeepEval/ACM each get an independent trajectory.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Relationship
  node_types RelationshipTransition
  edge_types advances_to
  state_types discovered
  state_types engaged
  state_types collaborated
  state_types adopted
  state_types converted
  internal_calculus ordered-stage monotone trajectory, per profile
  invariant a stage is reached only when recorded, with evidence; no silent regress
  invariant two relationships to one actor under different profiles are independent
  forbidden_inference contact -> relationship
  forbidden_inference relationship -> contract
  forbidden_inference collaboration on one profile -> standing on another
  native_format graf
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/relationship.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_relationship.py
  source_lineage capitalgym crm relationships

architecture shadow-institution
  canonical_name ShadowInstitutionGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Epistemic
  layer institutional
  semantic_question What do we know about an institution before any relationship or authority is established?
  purpose Epistemic knowledge of an institution pre-relationship: observed hierarchy, claim paths, public attachments, activation plan. NOT ForeignTwin (which models an externally-owned resource projection).
  maturity implemented
  node_types ShadowInstitutionNode
  node_types ObservedHierarchy
  node_types PublicAttachment
  edge_types observed_from
  edge_types converts_via
  state_types observed
  state_types shadow
  state_types relationship_established
  state_types active
  internal_calculus conversion staged by real relationship progress
  invariant conversion to active requires a relationship at >= collaborated, not a richer public picture
  forbidden_inference observed hierarchy -> established authority
  forbidden_inference public structure mapped -> relationship established
  native_format graf
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/shadow_institution.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_shadow_institution.py
  source_lineage SEED-A recursive organ document
